  "method": "Original B and companion embedded pixels only. The complete2MA6:11 he shows a shallow continuous left bar with an upper-right stamp linked by a narrow bridge and a separate lower-right stamp. The same-verse אשר literal hataf-patah supplies an explicit positive. Two same-page6:18 alef hataf-segol examples instead have three left stamps, and a literal same-font hataf-qamats has a deep left stem. Those discriminators support one U+05B2 insertion, independently challenged by a separate reviewer. The2MA7:40 detached lower rectangle has only a one-pixel bottom notch. Same-font literal bet-tsere has two detached stamps, while degraded patah may produce a joined bar with a notch; the saturated primary cannot decide. Retain that note. Five1MA qof omissions were revisited in complete primary/companion words, with ordinary and pointed same-page qof controls; their lower loop/leg region still does not distinguish the exact point or prove absence. That qof sweep is a word-level comparison, not a claim of five newly isolated readable points. Connected ink alone is not a rejection; missing diagnostic geometry is. Native and nearest-neighbor crops were freshly replayed from the original PDFs. No OCR, expected wording, grammar, sharpening or image reconstruction supplies any mark.",
